WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.380 --> 00:00:03.720
- [Announcer] The era of television.

00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:06.280
- [Announcer] The greatest
advance in television.

00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:10.200
- [Richard] In the '60s and
'70s, TV had become such an icon

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.430
that, that artists couldn't
resist just fooling with it.

00:00:13.430 --> 00:00:15.220
- It was all pretty much new,

00:00:15.220 --> 00:00:18.530
and it was really taking
sort of your standard TV sets

00:00:18.530 --> 00:00:20.620
and just making it really crazy.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.070
But the inherent vice of televisions

00:00:23.070 --> 00:00:25.650
is it is a consumer electronic.

00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.510
- Unlike painting and sculptures,

00:00:27.510 --> 00:00:31.710
these electronic pieces,
they could just go any time.

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:34.400
That was always the big
threat to this in a museum.

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:36.910
- [Jennifer] You have these
pieces that if it breaks down,

00:00:36.910 --> 00:00:37.830
what do you do?

00:00:37.830 --> 00:00:39.850
- The first person we call is CT Lui.

00:00:39.850 --> 00:00:42.410
- Lui's always been the
first person we go to.

00:00:42.410 --> 00:00:44.550
- It's because of my father,

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:47.330
they're able to be maintained,
they're able to be shown,

00:00:47.330 --> 00:00:50.410
they're able to be put out in the world.

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:51.580
- [Peter] Within the conservation field,

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:54.330
this is critically necessary.

00:00:54.330 --> 00:00:58.360
You can see just the enthusiasm
he has for this technology.

00:01:15.186 --> 00:01:17.769
(gentle music)

00:02:14.256 --> 00:02:16.839
(upbeat music)

00:02:32.051 --> 00:02:34.000
- [Jennifer] When people
started using video,

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.310
it was sort of this experimental media, so
everybody was sort of wanting

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:40.273
to know how it worked,
what you could do with it.

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:44.360
- Any major institution
that has video art,

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:46.853
probably my father has
touched in some way.

00:03:49.210 --> 00:03:50.460
- [Jennifer] The Whitney.

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:52.510
- [Jennifer] The Met.

